  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 215 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nSaturday and Sunday...Digging long wave upper trof acrs the \nPacific Northwest and ridging amplifying up the GRT LKS will \nresult in warming southwesterlies acrs the MID CONUS and toward \nthe GRT LKS. Saturday will be a full blown warm sector day with \nbreezy southerly winds and increasing thicknesses that support \nhighs in the 80s for much of the area. This may be a day of \nincreased cropland fire danger risk depending on humidity \ntrends. Then eyes turn to the tropical system in the Gulf and \nthe path it may take getting drawn northward inland. Models are\ngenerally in agreement on a more southeastward track that keeps \nmeasurable rain east of our outlook area.\n\nMonday On...A significant drop in temperatures is expected \nnext week as a seasonably strong cold front moves through the \nMidwest. Based on latest model guidance, the cold front is \nforecast to move through Monday night into Tuesday. Beyond \nMonday, the NBM is showing a large spread in max temps, with the\ncurrent mean forecast in the 60s across eastern Iowa and \nnorthwest Illinois. However, these values could trend lower with\n50s possible for highs across portions of the area. This mid \nweek cool down will be short-lived as the upstream upper trough\nand associated surface low ejects out toward the Upper Midwest.\nIf the pattern unfolds this way, unsettled weather looks on tap\nfor the middle/end of the week.",
